# recipe.env — all configuration for this recipe. Sourced by up.sh / install.sh / down.sh /
# view.sh through _config.sh. `recipe.env.local`, if present, is sourced AFTER this file and
# overrides it: put site values and experiments there.
#
# Two kinds of lines: SITE (change them) and LOAD-BEARING (each comment says what breaks).

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── SITE
# Head first, then worker. up.sh must run on the head. The head carries the HTTP server, the
# scheduler and the Ray control plane (~7 GiB heavier than the worker): size memory on the HEAD.
CLUSTER_NODES=10.0.0.1,10.0.0.2   # CHANGE ME

# The direct ConnectX link between the boxes, not the management LAN.
ETH_IF=enp1s0f0np0          # CHANGE ME: TCP side (Ray / gloo bootstrap)
IB_IF=rocep1s0f0            # CHANGE ME: RDMA device, as in /sys/class/infiniband
MASTER_PORT=29501

# Host paths, identical on both boxes.
HF_HOME=/srv/models/hf                        # CHANGE ME
CHECKPOINT_DIR=$HF_HOME/q38-nvfp4-nvidia      # the download
SERVED_DIR=$HF_HOME/q38-nvfp4-w4a16           # built by tools/make-w4a16-variant.py

CONTAINER_NAME=vllm_node
IMAGE=q38-nvfp4-w4a16
# Bind address of the OpenAI API. The container uses --network host, so 0.0.0.0 exposes it on
# every NIC, and the API is unauthenticated unless VLLM_API_KEY is set. Measurements were taken
# with 0.0.0.0 behind a private network; the loopback default was booted from a fresh clone
# with identical results (docs/HARDWARE.md).
HOST=127.0.0.1
PORT=8000

# ────────────────────────────────────────── LOAD-BEARING: NCCL / interconnect
# Upstream keeps these in a gitignored .env. Without them NCCL falls back to TCP on the same
# cable and every step is ~2x slower, silently. Proof of RDMA during a generation:
# /sys/class/infiniband/$IB_IF/ports/1/counters/port_xmit_data moves while the TCP tx counter
# of $ETH_IF stays flat (measured on 700 tokens: RDMA +1751.8 MB, TCP +0.2 MB). ./view.sh
# prints both.
CONTAINER_NCCL_IB_DISABLE=0
CONTAINER_NCCL_IB_HCA=rocep1s0f0            # CHANGE ME: = IB_IF
CONTAINER_NCCL_IB_GID_INDEX=3
CONTAINER_NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME=enp1s0f0np0    # CHANGE ME: = ETH_IF
CONTAINER_GLOO_SOCKET_IFNAME=enp1s0f0np0    # CHANGE ME: = ETH_IF
CONTAINER_NCCL_NVLS_ENABLE=0
CONTAINER_NCCL_NET_GDR_DISABLE=1            # GB10: GPU memory is host memory; GDR hangs

# ─────────────────────────────────── LOAD-BEARING: sm_121 correctness (not tuning)
CONTAINER_VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_MOE_INT4=0    # FlashInfer int4 MoE returns garbage on sm_121
CONTAINER_VLLM_MOE_USE_DEEP_GEMM=0          # no sm_121 path
CONTAINER_VLLM_MARLIN_USE_ATOMIC_ADD=1
CONTAINER_HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
# Read and ignored by this vLLM (only the --attention-backend flag acts). Kept because it is in
# the configuration all numbers were measured on.
CONTAINER_VLLM_ATTENTION_BACKEND=TRITON_ATTN

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────── the four flags that decide
# 1. W4A16 on the routed experts. Marlin is the only W4A16 path the sm_121 oracle offers; the
#    five ranked ahead are W4A4. Also a canary: an unquantized MTP MoE makes vLLM refuse to boot
#    instead of serving with dead speculation. Verify in the engine echo: 'moe_backend': 'marlin'.
MOE_BACKEND=marlin

# 2. The 47.68 GiB n-gram table stays FP8. Without this AND mods/ple-fp8-mixed it is allocated
#    bf16 (95.43 GiB): OOM on both ranks.
VLLM_QWEN4EXP_PLE_FP8=1

# 3. Pins the KV pool and skips memory profiling. Without it vLLM fills gmu 0.85 with KV,
#    MemAvailable falls to ~1.6 GiB and the kernel OOM-kills ray::RayWorkerProc under load
#    (observed 2026-09-06). 26 GiB = 3,547,511 tokens (fp8 KV), ~11 GiB headroom on the head.
#    Context costs ~7.7 GiB per million tokens at 5 streams (derived). Re-measure MemAvailable
#    on BOTH ranks before raising.
KV_BYTES=27917287424        # 26 GiB

# 4. Legal only while SPEC_TOKENS > 0: KV block size is 1664 = 13 x 128 with MTP, 1600 without,
#    and the engine refuses after loading the weights. Remove if SPEC_TOKENS=0.
#    EXTRA_ARGS carries exactly ONE flag (word-split inside upstream's docker run line).
EXTRA_ARGS=--prefix-match-unit=128

# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── serving parameters
KV_DTYPE=fp8_e4m3           # see the KV block below
GPU_MEM_UTIL=0.85           # no longer sizes the pool with KV_BYTES set, but up.sh derives its
                            # pre-boot abort threshold from it: lowering it relaxes that guard
MAX_LEN=700000              # per-request cap, via YaRN
ROPE_FACTOR=2.6702880859375 # minimum exact factor for 700000 (262144 * f >= MAX_LEN; 2.67 raises)
MAX_SEQS=8
BATCHED_TOKENS=4096         # prefill chunk. 8192 measured: TTFT +97 % at c=3, aggregate -20 %
LONG_PREFILL=4096           # long-prefill threshold, kept equal to the chunk
SPEC_TOKENS=3               # MTP draft width. K=4: accepted length +11 %, aggregate -7 % at c=4
EP=1
MAMBA_DTYPE=bfloat16
CG=1
CG_SIZES=4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32   # do not widen: the CAPTURE PEAK OOM-kills, not the residual
IDX_SHARE=1
VLLM_DEEP_GEMM_WARMUP=skip

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── KV cache in FP8
# Configuration on which every number in README.md was measured.
# Per-token K/V cost 14,144 -> 7,696 bytes (x1.84): 26 GiB hold 3,547,511 tokens measured,
# against ~1.97 M derived for bf16.
# Cost: about -12 % decode throughput at 700 k of context, ~0 at short context; and
# mods/qsa-kv-fp8 rewrites four files of the installed vLLM, one of them the attention backend.
# Safety:
#  - the patch anchors guard the ENGINE version (exact-count match, exit non-zero on drift).
#    Nothing guards the CHECKPOINT: a wider K/V dynamic range would saturate e4m3 and return
#    wrong tokens with every anchor matching.
#  - the headroom figure (|K|max 89.5, |V|max 31.4 against 448) was measured 2026-08-28 on the
#    FP8 build, NOT on this NVFP4 checkpoint. Run overlay/mods/qsa-kv-fp8/probe/ on the served
#    checkpoint (docs/MODS.md) and read the absmax against 448.
#  - logprob MAE vs bf16 KV: +0.2265 nat on short prompts. tools/logprobs-mae.py flags it
#    (0.05 nat threshold), correctly: the arithmetic changes on purpose. Neither figure
#    measures output quality.
# Fallback without the attention patch, in recipe.env.local:
#     KV_DTYPE=bfloat16
#     VLLM_QSA_KV_FP8=0
# Expected ~1.97 M tokens for the same 26 GiB. Not booted; no number.
VLLM_QSA_KV_FP8=1
